Subject: read musl-locales definitions from /usr/share/i18n/locales/musl

The Region & Language KCM offers only the locales whose definition files
it finds in this directory. musl-locales installs them in musl/ below
it, so the directory holds no file, the KCM lists no format locale, and
it reports that localectl could not list them.

Chimera Linux carries the same one-line change for the same layout.

--- a/kcms/region_language/glibclocaleconstructor.cpp
+++ b/kcms/region_language/glibclocaleconstructor.cpp
@@ -156,7 +156,7 @@
 
 QString GlibcLocaleConstructor::localeFileDirPath()
 {
-    return QStringLiteral("/usr/share/i18n/locales");
+    return QStringLiteral("/usr/share/i18n/locales/musl");
 }
 
 QString GlibcLocaleConstructor::failedFindLocalesMessage()
